WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.234
-Chip and Joanna, welcome back.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.467
It's always great to see you.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.033
What does a typical
Valentine's Day

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:06.467
look like for you guys?

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.467
-We typically, during the week,

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.334
we'll go on
a date night Thursday.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:12.334
So when Valentine's
comes around,

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:13.501
we like to include the kids.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:16.133
So, we'll do
a fancy dinner at home.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.934
Steak, lobster --
-All the kids write each other

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.667
Valentine's letters.
-They all get dressed up.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:24.000
So, we did it a little earlier
since we were gonna be here,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.667
but it's our favorite thing.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.000
-Well, happy Valentine's Day.
I'm glad that you're here.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.901
-Fallon --
Fallontine's Day.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.400
-Thank you.
Fallontine's Day.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.133
It's amazing.
-That's exactly right.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.200
Thank you.
-Thank you for having us, Jimmy.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.701
What an honor.
-You two --

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.701
-There's nothing more romantic

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.334
than being on "The Fallon Show"
on Valentine's Day...

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.601
-True.
-Yes.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:46.534
-...and the show title being
"Fallontine's Day."

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:49.133
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-This is a high bar

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.434
for me to try to beat next year.
-We did this for you.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.734
-Well, I want to talk to
you guys about how you met.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:57.400
Because it involves a person
called Hot John.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.868
-Poor John.
-I hope he's watching.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.567
This will be amazing.
-How did you meet,

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:04.033
and what did Hot John
have to do with any of this?

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.834
-Well, I worked for my dad
at his tire shop for 10 years.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.634
So I'm selling tires.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.200
His roommate
was there getting tires.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.367
-Hot John.
-Hot John.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.968
-Okay.
That's your roommate.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.701
-Yeah, so all the guys that work
at the tire shop, all the time,

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.400
would try to set me up
with the customers.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.300
And I'd always say,
"Y'all, leave me alone."

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.734
But this time it felt different.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.267
They're like, "There's this
really good-looking guy.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:27.100
His name is John. If you just
walk through the showroom

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.501
and to the waiting room,
just go talk to him."

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.801
-He's wandering.
-Yes.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.400
He's just sitting there,
waiting for his tires.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.801
So I got the courage to get up,
out of my office.

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:41.501
I walk towards the waiting room,
and John and I make eye contact.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.634
But I'm not really gifted
at making conversation.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.033
-That's true.
-So I looked at him,

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.934
and I was like, "Now what?"
and so, instead of the going

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.801
to the waiting room,
I walk straight outside,

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.667
like I was gonna take
a smoke break or something.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:56.834
As I'm walking outside, Chip is
coming in to get Hot John.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.367
And he intersects.
-Inadvertently.

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:02.167
-Yep, and unlike her,
I'm incredible at eye contact.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.767
[ Laughter ]
I always have a one-liner

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.400
planned for any occasion
where you might meet

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.234
one of the most beautiful women
on the planet.

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:13.100
You must have that
back-pocket line ready to rock.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.100
And so she walked right past
Hot John, thankfully,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.167
right into the loving arms...
-Awkwardly.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.901
-You know, John's tall,
dark, and handsome.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:23.300
I was sort of shorter,
redder, and frumpier.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.634
[ Laughter ]
-That's my type.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:25.801
I was sort of the opposite end
of the spectrum.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.067
Jo and I chatted
for a few minutes,

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:31.400
and before you know it,
the love was in the air.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.634
-Oh, my gosh.
[ Applause ]

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:36.634
Well, I'm so happy.
You are about to celebrate

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:39.133
your 20th wedding anniversary.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:41.100
You're 20th wedding anniversary
this May.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.501
-Two decades.
-Congratulations.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:45.534
-Oh, my gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:49.434
She looks like the day -- like
the day we got married there.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:51.033
-Well, this is --
It's fitting you're back

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:52.334
in New York,
because this is actually

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:53.734
where you went on your
honeymoon, correct?

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:56.400
-Honeymoon. A lot of anniversary
trips are here in New York.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.033
-Yeah, Jo has always
loved this city.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:01.801
It's always meant a lot to her.
She interned, back in the day,

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:04.601
under Dan Rather,
which was a cool honor for us

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.100
and our community.
You know, the whole thing.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.067
She was, like, legendary.
That me bumping into her,

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:12.834
you know, fortuitously,
it's like, she was the one.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.267
She was the catch
in the whole area.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:18.868
-Well, didn't you name one of
your children after a hotel?

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:22.601
-The Drake Hotel.
That's where we honeymooned

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.834
and then our anniversary.
-We have a strange --

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:27.501
It's like the Midas touch,
where it's sort of

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.100
the opposite end
of the spectrum.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.267
Every place
that we sort of, like --

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:34.534
that means the world to us,
from a relationship standpoint,

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:36.400
those places
all go out of business.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.567
So, the Drake hotel,
we stayed in,

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:40.868
and it was
this sort of legendary hotel.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.267
-It's no longer there.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.434
-But we came back to it, like,
years later,

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:47.200
and it no longer exists.
-Laser tag, huh?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.434
-Maybe they moved.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.367
-It's like a Hilton
or something.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.801
-Maybe.
-Time to have another kid.

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:55.334
-That's true.
-Tell them. Tell them.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.334
-[ Barks ]
-Oh, my God. Just barking.

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.701
-In our ecosystem,
anytime someone says sort of

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:04.501
an edgy joke like that,
we start chanting, "Number six!

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:06.767
Number six!"
'Cause we got five.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:09.300
So if anybody wants
to go along with this,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.667
if Jimmy says something like you
should maybe have another child,

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:16.033
then, "Number six!
Number six! Number six!"

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.934
-I like it.
-Number six! Number six!

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:20.701
-You don't like it at all, no.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:23.734
-Can we talk about -- because I
know you have five kids now.

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.400
-Yes.
-And I know you bond over

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.968
Taylor Swift with your
daughters. Right?

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.767
Do you want to tell
the Taylor Swift story?

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:34.267
-I would love to tell it.
-You were there.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.701
You were there, Jimmy.
-Was I?

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:39.200
-We were in New York.
We somehow gotten invited

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.801
to this thing called
"The Times 100."

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.334
And I thought
it was segmented out.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.167
This is true.
I thought it was segmented out,

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.267
like, around --
like, regionally.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:50.934
So I thought we were
the 100 most influential people

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:52.868
in Central Texas.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.467
But they, in fact,
meant, like, a larger spot.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:58.000
-Yes, yes.
-A larger audience than that.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.667
So we come to this thing,
everybody's there.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.133
You were there.
You remember.

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.267
2019.
-2019.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:06.467
-Of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:07.667
-You were sitting
in front of us.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.634
-Oh, of course.
Yeah, like it was yesterday.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.534
Whenever Timberlake
says something,

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.167
you know exactly
what he's talking about.

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:14.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:16.234
But if I mention
some bro moment,

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.434
you have no idea
what I'm talking about.

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:19.767
-We were bro'ing out?
-We were bro'd out, bro.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.901
-Really?
-So, long story short,

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.667
we're in an auditorium
similar to this.

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.300
-Oh, I remember this!
-Taylor Swift comes in.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.267
The whole audience is filled.
-But everyone was mingling.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.868
Everyone's mingling. There was
The Rock, Martha Stewart.

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:33.367
We were in awe. We were two kids
from Waco, Texas.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:34.701
"What the heck
are we doing here?"

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:37.133
-I flirted with Martha Stewart
in an aggressive --

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:38.501
in a very real way.
-Yeah, you did.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.100
[ Laughter ]
-"In an aggressive way."

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.701
-I told her, "If anything
ever happens to Jo..."

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.968
-Oh, gosh.
-"...you better watch your DMs."

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:49.334
-Come on.
20 years now in May.

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:51.334
20 years in May.
So, Taylor walks in the room.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:52.601
-She walks in.
-All the oxygen...

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:55.067
-And the room goes silent.
Do you remember?

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:56.667
Were you in the --
And she walks in,

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:59.133
and all of us just --
[ Gasps ] -- take a breath in.

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:03.234
-And when you're sitting next to
The Rock, and you see him gasp

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:05.968
about this amazing creature,
we were just like,

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:07.801
"Who in the world --
Who came in?"

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.133
We weren't even
paying attention.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:11.300
Taylor Swift rolls in.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.334
She kind of catches eye contact
with, I thought, me.

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:17.000
But Jo swears
to this day it was her.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.234
This is true.
And she goes like this to us.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.901
-But we both thought it's,
for sure, someone behind us.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:25.367
-We're looking
over our shoulders.

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:27.033
[ Laughter ]
-Like idiots.

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:28.267
-Wondering, "Who in the world
is talking to?"

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:29.968
-And I was like, "Me?"
-And how hilarious,

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:32.400
'cause, Jimmy, you were actually
in the front row

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.734
where the real celebrities were.
-Yeah.

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.334
-And we were
a little further back up.

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:37.934
We were, like, back row.
-Please.

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.734
-And maybe
she was doing it to you.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:40.968
-Wow!
-Who's to say?

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.734
It was one of us three,
for sure.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:45.601
-Yeah, I do remember.
"Is that Taylor?" Yeah.

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:47.367
-Let's go, let's go.
-Taylor loves one of us.

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:50.300
Yeah, all right. But let's
go ahead and believe that.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.267
-There you go.
-It made our day.

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:54.267
We were thrilled.
We were smitten.

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:56.434
-How cool is she
to just even do that?

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:58.901
-Oh, yeah, she sends us
these little gift baskets

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:00.767
whenever she releases
one of her albums.

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:03.601
-She's the classiest.
She's the tops.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:06.501
I think I remember this
because this is around

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:08.601
when you were kind of
launching your network.

00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:09.834
Do you remember that?
You were here,

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:11.133
and you were talking to me,
you're like,

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:13.100
"We're not sure if we're
legally allowed to say."

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.100
-We were so scared.
-And I think you were not

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.267
legally allowed to say it,
but Chip did.

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:18.801
-I said it.
-Of course, right before

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:20.267
we came out, they said,
"Don't mention it, Chip."

00:07:20.267 --> 00:07:22.834
-The final word,
"Do not announce the network."

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:24.934
-Which then makes him go,
"Got it."

00:07:24.934 --> 00:07:26.400
-"Well, I've got to announce
the network now."

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.267
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:30.701
-It was serious.
-And so -- we were nervous.

00:07:30.701 --> 00:07:33.467
We were nervous that we were
gonna go offstage to handcuffs.

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:35.133
We don't even know
if this is a real thing.

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:36.667
-Now it's a massive hit.

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:38.367
I'm obsessed
with Magnolia Network.

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:39.834
I love it so much.
-Thank you.

00:07:39.834 --> 00:07:42.601
-I'll tell you what I like.
I like "Maine Cabin Masters."

00:07:42.601 --> 00:07:44.501
-Yeah, they're the best.
-I love that show.

00:07:44.501 --> 00:07:46.300
I think it's just feel-good.
I love it.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.734
I love to see what they do.
They're brilliant.

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:48.901
They're geniuses.
-Totally.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.734
-I love the whole beginning, end
of that stuff.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:53.033
I love that.
I love "Magnolia Table."

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:55.934
-Thank you.
-I love "The Lost Kitchen."

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:57.901
-Yeah. Let's go.
-"Lost Kitchen."

00:07:57.901 --> 00:07:59.834
-Let's go.
-When you watch one show

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:02.434
on Magnolia Network, there's
commercials for other shows.

00:08:02.434 --> 00:08:05.300
And I go, "Honey, we gotta start
DVR'ing that one."

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:09.501
So, I'm basically watch
the network 24/7 now, nonstop.

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:12.133
But I want to go through
"The Lost Kitchen."

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.567
I want to work there.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:15.734
-What a dream.
-They're brilliant people.

00:08:15.734 --> 00:08:17.100
-I know.
-But congratulations.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:21.734
-You have to fill out a postcard
to even get a reservation.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.801
-You have to send them
a postcard.

00:08:23.801 --> 00:08:25.367
-Yes.
-She gets thousands,

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:26.968
so she's like, "Ugh."
-And she's so cool.

00:08:26.968 --> 00:08:29.300
It's just the best.
Can we talk about your book,

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.200
as well, by the way?
I'm into this.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.133
I just finished
Matthew McConaughey's book,

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:34.934
and it was very inspiring
for me and moving.

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:37.133
And I'm ready
for another one like this.

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:38.534
And it's perfect.

00:08:38.534 --> 00:08:40.200
I'm moving right into this.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.100
You almost didn't release this
and publish this.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.634
-Yeah.
-What was it?

00:08:43.634 --> 00:08:46.701
It was just an exercise?
-It was me moving into

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:48.801
my mid 40s,
feeling like everything

00:08:48.801 --> 00:08:49.934
was a little bit foggy.

00:08:49.934 --> 00:08:52.634
And I told Chip,
"I need to look at my life.

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:54.801
I need to evaluate it
and really --"

00:08:54.801 --> 00:08:56.667
I felt like I was at this
emotional threshold,

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:58.968
really trying to figure out,
"What do I need to bring with me

00:08:58.968 --> 00:09:01.133
as I move forward?
What served me well?"

00:09:01.133 --> 00:09:03.667
And then, "What doubts
and insecurities and fears

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:04.834
do I just need to leave behind

00:09:04.834 --> 00:09:06.968
as I move forward
in this new season?"

00:09:06.968 --> 00:09:09.667
But I also think,
if you take off that jacket,

00:09:09.667 --> 00:09:14.200
there's me as a 6-year-old.
And a lot of my writing

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.067
in that practice
was writing back to her.

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:20.234
I feel like as we get older,
we chase maturity and wisdom.

00:09:20.234 --> 00:09:22.467
And I think all that's great,
but I think we also forget

00:09:22.467 --> 00:09:24.667
that child-like spirit
we all once had.

00:09:24.667 --> 00:09:26.734
And so I was trying
to get back to her.

00:09:26.734 --> 00:09:29.534
That's, like, the wholist I was,
the freeist I was.

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:31.334
And so a lot of the writing

00:09:31.334 --> 00:09:33.467
was writing back
to my 6-year-old self.

00:09:33.467 --> 00:09:35.801
-Let's go!
-But I want to ask you --

00:09:35.801 --> 00:09:38.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love that.

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:42.534
-I love asking this question.

00:09:42.534 --> 00:09:45.033
Because there's something about
that child-like wonder

00:09:45.033 --> 00:09:47.100
that we all had.
-Yeah.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:51.567
-Jimmy, what would you tell
your 6-year-old self?

00:09:51.567 --> 00:09:54.934
-Well, I actually
thought you might ask that.

00:09:54.934 --> 00:09:56.100
-Okay, so you're prepared.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.601
-I have a photo of me
when I was 6.

00:09:58.601 --> 00:10:04.133
So, I'll talk to myself.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:10:04.133 --> 00:10:06.334
-Aye-aye, Captain.
-What a doll.

00:10:06.334 --> 00:10:07.868
[ Applause ]
-Jimmy...

00:10:07.868 --> 00:10:11.868
Jimmy, you've served four years
in the U.S. Navy.

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:13.501
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.501 --> 00:10:17.968
-You're a patriot and a hero
at 6 years old.

00:10:17.968 --> 00:10:23.100
I would say,
it's all gonna be okay.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.701
-Yeah.
-It's all gonna work out

00:10:24.701 --> 00:10:26.200
pretty awesomely, by the way.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.100
You're gonna make
millions of people laugh.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.934
-Wow.
-You're gonna work with some of

00:10:29.934 --> 00:10:33.200
your biggest idols,
and your wife is pretty hot.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.400
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, I love it!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love it.

00:10:37.334 --> 00:10:39.934
-Whoo whoo whoo whoo!

00:10:39.934 --> 00:10:41.901
-The book is awesome.
I'm loving it.

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:44.601
I'm loving everything
I'm reading so far.

00:10:44.601 --> 00:10:48.267
Not only is it interesting
but it helps other people.

00:10:48.267 --> 00:10:50.367
It helps me. It helps you
when you read this book.

00:10:50.367 --> 00:10:51.968
And I think everyone here
is going to love it because

00:10:51.968 --> 00:10:54.267
you brought one for everyone
in our audience tonight.

00:10:54.267 --> 00:10:56.934
You're all going home
with a copy.

00:10:56.934 --> 00:10:58.968
That's what I'm talking about,
right here!

00:10:58.968 --> 00:11:00.667
We love when you're here!

00:11:00.667 --> 00:11:02.501
Please come back!

00:11:02.501 --> 00:11:03.968
Chip and Joanna Gaines!

00:11:03.968 --> 00:11:07.300
"The Stories We Tell"
is available now!

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:09.133
We'll be right back
with Rhett and Link!

00:11:09.133 --> 00:11:10.968
Stick around! Yeah!
Come on!

